## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/chromakey.html
- Summary (EN): The Chroma Key node removes parts of an image whose hue, saturation and luminance fall within defined ranges by setting their alpha to zero. It isolates a foreground subject from a green screen.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Chroma Key retire les zones d'une image dont la teinte, la saturation et la luminance tombent dans des plages choisies, pour isoler un sujet sur fond vert.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the original layer to key"]

- Key parameters: ["Method: legacy Chromakey or Channel Separation key", "Invert: inverts the resulting matte", "Hue / Saturation: hue and saturation ranges to key, sampled with an eyedropper", "Luminance Range: luminance range to key", "Screen Color: colour to key out (Channel Separation only)", "Threshold and Width: matte threshold and range on both sides (Channel Separation only)", "Rolloff (Hue, Saturation, Luminance): soft falloff extending each range, with Interpolation curve (linear, ease in, ease out, smooth, Gaussian)", "Preview and Preview Color: tints the keyed result without removing pixels", "Premultiply: multiplies the input by the generated matte"]

- Caveats: ["Screen Color, Threshold and Width apply only when Method is Channel Separation", "Preview does not key out pixels, it only colours the result", "Premultiply permanently discards keyed-out pixels; use the matte output to process the matte first"]

